  "why": "OB6 (open-plots build-out, G978): Mosslight Ruins' 8 x 8 grid of 62.5 m tiles after round 62's top-down (art/grid/round-62-open-plot-palettes/19-mosslight-ruins.jpg): the ruined tower on its outcrop at the plaza, lanes to the four entries, an L of emerald pools (E) hugging each corner of the plaza, ruin courts (R) round them and flanking the four road entries, mossy gardens (G) at the side entries and in the gaps (look loop R3: the inner ring was Night Market gardens and the entries its kiosk forecourts). Mirror-symmetric: each row reads the same from either end, the south half the north turned twice. The landmark is take A (Hunyuan3D 2.1, art/mosslight-ruins/round-1-landmark/); its window faces glow emerald as landmark.glow triangles.",
